  "text": "A person who controls a machine or vehicle.\n\nTaken food into the mouth and swallowed it.\n\nMoved or carried by water in this sentence.\n\nPut something into a boat or other carrier.\n\nSparkFest’s story studio · Meet Jo and Loop\n\nBelonging to or happening during the night.\n\nPeople talking and listening to each other.\n\nMade something untidy by moving it lightly.\n\nCreating something or causing it to happen.\n\nDirects the eyes, or appears a certain way.\n\nIntroduces the second part of a comparison.\n\nA particular form of a story or other work.\n\nTell a story or describe what is happening.\n\nTilted something so its contents moved out.\n\nThe part of a plant that opens into petals.\n\nA place where things are kept until needed.\n\nSmall amounts of liquid falling separately.\n\nin the prepared spot, waiting to be covered\n\nUsing your voice so the words can be heard.\n\nColors that identify the two boat landings.\n\nwaiting for your steering or docking action\n\nA series of musical notes forming a melody.\n\nTaking something from one place to another.\n\nWhy do the loaves need to be similar sizes?\n\nAt the usual time · Pip reads Mara’s story\n\nThe complete story, from beginning to end.\n\nYou steer the boat · Pip waits on the bank\n\ncrossing. Choose Place section to keep it.\n\nPaused because you were unsure what to do.\n\nReturning to an earlier place or position.\n\nPut a seed into the soil so it could grow.\n\nFor more time or distance than the others.\n\nRead at your own pace; your page is saved.\n\nAn entrance that can be opened and closed.\n\nThe crossing is ready for everyone to use.\n\nPip takes the seed back into his backpack.\n\nA Small Repair · Sol’s original manuscript\n\nWhat a word, sentence or action expresses.\n\nTogether with someone, or using something.\n\nPeople who know and care about each other.",
  "textSha256": "73bf71092a40c33167ea2e0800d7f9072bf8475b19b29c05e8c160c386e6753e",
